1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,917
Excuse me, I was told to come here for advice about, erm, Management Diploma

2
00:00:06,917 --> 00:00:07,380
courses?

3
00:00:07,380 --> 00:00:09,420
You've certainly come to the right place.

4
00:00:09,420 --> 00:00:11,500
Hi, my name is Monica.

5
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:13,188
Nice to meet you.

6
00:00:13,188 --> 00:00:15,720
My name is Andrew, Andrew Harris.

7
00:00:15,720 --> 00:00:20,840
So, Andrew, have you seen our diploma course prospectus yet?

8
00:00:20,840 --> 00:00:23,091
Yes, I've already looked at it.

9
00:00:23,091 --> 00:00:27,592
In fact, I thought the information on course content was really useful,

10
00:00:27,592 --> 00:00:32,844
but I'm afraid I'm a bit confused by all the different ways you can

11
00:00:32,844 --> 00:00:33,969
do the course:

12
00:00:33,969 --> 00:00:36,220
full-time intensive, part-time and so on.

13
00:00:36,220 --> 00:00:39,142
Well, let's see if I can help.

14
00:00:39,142 --> 00:00:43,316
I think each course type has its advantages and disadvantages,

15
00:00:43,316 --> 00:00:47,491
so it really depends on you- your own study habits,

16
00:00:47,491 --> 00:00:49,995
and your financial circumstances, of course.

17
00:00:49,995 --> 00:00:52,500
Are you working at the moment?

18
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:52,851
Yes.

19
00:00:52,851 --> 00:00:57,761
I've been working in the administration section of the local hospital for the last

20
00:00:57,761 --> 00:00:58,463
three years.

21
00:00:58,463 --> 00:01:03,373
And before that I worked in the office of a computer engineering company for

22
00:01:03,373 --> 00:01:04,075
two years.

23
00:01:04,075 --> 00:01:07,582
So, I've got about five years of relevant work experience.

24
00:01:07,582 --> 00:01:11,090
And what I'm hoping to focus on is Personnel Management.

25
00:01:11,090 --> 00:01:11,778
I see.

26
00:01:11,778 --> 00:01:15,561
And are you planning to leave your current job to study,

27
00:01:15,561 --> 00:01:19,000
or are you thinking about just taking a year off?

28
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:22,026
I want to know what my options are, really.

29
00:01:22,026 --> 00:01:26,733
I don't want to quit my job or anything and my employers are keen

30
00:01:26,733 --> 00:01:31,439
for me to get some more qualifications but obviously, it would be better if

31
00:01:31,439 --> 00:01:35,810
I could do a course without taking too much time away from work.

32
00:01:35,810 --> 00:01:36,192
Right,

33
00:01:36,192 --> 00:01:40,400
so you don't really want to do the full-time course, then?

34
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:41,377
No, not really.

35
00:01:41,377 --> 00:01:43,331
It's also a question of finances.

36
00:01:43,331 --> 00:01:47,890
You see, my office have agreed to pay the cost of the course itself,

37
00:01:47,890 --> 00:01:52,449
but I would have to take unpaid leave if I want to study full-time

38
00:01:52,449 --> 00:01:57,007
and, well, I don't think I could afford to support myself with no salary

39
00:01:57,007 --> 00:01:58,310
for a whole year.

40
00:01:58,310 --> 00:01:58,663
OK.

41
00:01:58,663 --> 00:02:00,782
Well, you have two other possibilities:

42
00:02:00,782 --> 00:02:05,373
you could either do the part-time course that would be over two years

43
00:02:05,373 --> 00:02:10,318
and you wouldn't have to take any time off work-or you could do what

44
00:02:10,318 --> 00:02:12,084
we call a 'modular' course.

45
00:02:12,084 --> 00:02:17,028
You could do that in eighteen months if you wanted-or longer, it's quite flexible

46
00:02:17,028 --> 00:02:19,500
and it would be up to you.

47
00:02:19,500 --> 00:02:20,000
Mmm.

48
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:23,500
So what does the part-time course involve?

49
00:02:23,500 --> 00:02:28,424
For that you would join an evening class and have a lecture twice a

50
00:02:28,424 --> 00:02:28,776
week.

51
00:02:28,776 --> 00:02:33,700
Then, you'd have to attend a seminar or discussion workshop one weekend a month.

52
00:02:33,700 --> 00:02:36,380
What kind of coursework would I have to do?

53
00:02:36,380 --> 00:02:37,670
Well, it's a mixture.

54
00:02:37,670 --> 00:02:40,573
You'd be expected to write an essay each month,

55
00:02:40,573 --> 00:02:42,508
which counts towards your final assessment.

56
00:02:42,508 --> 00:02:46,701
You have a case study to do by the end of the course,

57
00:02:46,701 --> 00:02:49,927
which might involve doing a survey or something like that,

58
00:02:49,927 --> 00:02:54,120
and also you need to hand in a short report every four weeks.

59
00:02:54,120 --> 00:02:54,469
So,

60
00:02:54,469 --> 00:02:59,008
that's quite a lot of work, then, on top of working every day.

61
00:02:59,008 --> 00:03:02,150
It sounds like a lot of studying-and really tiring.

62
00:03:02,150 --> 00:03:07,300
Yes, you certainly wouldn't have much free time!

63
00:03:07,300 --> 00:03:08,915
What about the 'modular' course?

64
00:03:08,915 --> 00:03:11,500
What would I have to do for that?

65
00:03:11,500 --> 00:03:15,735
That's where you get the opportunity to study full-time for short periods.

66
00:03:15,735 --> 00:03:19,971
That way you can cover a lot of coursework and attend lectures

67
00:03:19,971 --> 00:03:21,735
and seminars during the day.

68
00:03:21,735 --> 00:03:26,676
And each module lasts for one term, say, about twelve weeks at a time.

69
00:03:26,676 --> 00:03:31,618
There are obvious advantages in this-the main one being that you can study in

70
00:03:31,618 --> 00:03:33,382
a much more intensive way,

71
00:03:33,382 --> 00:03:35,500
which suits some people much better.

72
00:03:35,500 --> 00:03:39,868
And how many of these 'modules' would I have to do to get the

73
00:03:39,868 --> 00:03:40,180
diploma?

74
00:03:40,180 --> 00:03:44,384
The current programme is two modules-and then you have to choose a topic to

75
00:03:44,384 --> 00:03:47,688
work in more depth-but you can base that on your job,

76
00:03:47,688 --> 00:03:50,991
and so you don't need to be away from the office,

77
00:03:50,991 --> 00:03:53,694
and how long it takes is up to you.

78
00:03:53,694 --> 00:03:57,297
The important thing is that you don't have to study and work.

79
00:03:57,297 --> 00:04:00,000
You can focus on one thing at a time.

80
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:01,667
Yes, I can see that.

81
00:04:01,667 --> 00:04:03,000
It certainly sounds attractive!

82
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:05,000
It would be more expensive, though.

83
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:09,000
I mean, I'd have to support myself without pay for each module.

84
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:09,653
That's true,

85
00:04:09,653 --> 00:04:12,267
so that might be a problem for you.

86
00:04:12,267 --> 00:04:15,860
Look, why don't you talk this over with your employers and...
